    },
    "findings": [
      "This package is an active synchronous filesystem/HMAC audit-ledger sink with mutable private state and injected key custody, not outbound network filtering.",
      "flush drains the ring before HMAC, JSON serialization and append; failures after drain lose staged records despite the never-drop claim.",
      "records.join(\"\\n\") does not authenticate record boundaries; [\"a\",\"b\"] and [\"a\\nb\"] share a MAC preimage, while unsigned count adjustment can satisfy length checks.",
      "Construction resets sequence and genesis even when appending an existing ledger; verification accepts empty chains and valid prefixes without a trusted expected head/count.",
      "Non-strict mode permits the public zero key; nonzero short/predictable keys are accepted and injected key arrays are retained without copying. Epoch adoption flushes under the old key before switching and does not authorize rotation.",
      "readEgressLedger propagates malformed JSON and non-ENOENT I/O errors, parsed batches are not structurally validated, and HardenedBorderViolation is not used to wrap filesystem failures.",
      "RingBuffer bounds slots rather than record bytes, does not zeroize payloads and allocates a new drain array; preserve FIFO/backpressure, identity, allocation and error behavior.",
      "The two Fungi assets cover only the ledger filename and host-computed chain/epoch/config decision folds; they do not implement crypto, durable writes, ring state or end-to-end authority."
    ],
    "materialObligations": [
      "Preserve failure/recovery semantics and resolve drain-before-append record loss before any authority claim.",
      "Bind record boundaries/count into the authenticated framing and preserve exact UTF-8/HMAC/JSONL behavior.",
      "Preserve restart/completeness policy, expected-head/count checks, key custody/rotation and legacy/epoch verification rules.",
      "Preserve ring capacity/backpressure, object identity, allocation limits, error prototypes/codes and filesystem error behavior.",
      "Keep existing Fungi assets non-authorizing and retain TypeScript as the consumer shadow."
    ]
  },
